{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#932","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#932","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#932\",\"parent_revision\":\"276b2bff220ec175d094203420f0ddd80cd83a81c17c9dfd0b6cefb29487eb7b\",\"root_revision\":\"276b2bff220ec175d094203420f0ddd80cd83a81c17c9dfd0b6cefb29487eb7b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd wave/item/merge event logging to plan/milestone-{N}-telemetry.jsonl during /work-milestone execution. Track wave-start, wave-complete, item-start, item-complete, item-blocked, merge-attempt, merge-success, merge-conflict, gate-pass, gate-fail. Build uv run sam telemetry report command. Adapted from Citadel telemetry-log.cjs concept.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | Event types specified | AVAILABLE \u2014 issue description lists all 10 events |\\n| 2 | Log format | DERIVABLE \u2014 JSONL is standard; schema per event type derivable from event names |\\n| 3 | Log path convention | AVAILABLE \u2014 `plan/milestone-{N}-telemetry.jsonl` |\\n| 4 | `sam telemetry report` CLI integration point | DERIVABLE \u2014 `sam` CLI is in `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/` or `packages/sam_schema/`; add `telemetry` subcommand |\\n| 5 | Emission points in `/work-milestone` skill | DERIVABLE \u2014 read skill execution flow; emit at wave dispatch, item completion, merge steps, gate checks |\\n| 6 | Append vs. overwrite semantics | AVAILABLE \u2014 append (multiple runs accumulate history) |\\n| 7 | Citadel telemetry-log.cjs as prior art | AVAILABLE \u2014 concept adapted from this reference |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 all conditions AVAILABLE or DERIVABLE. Standard telemetry logging pattern.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. Adds observability to milestone execution. 2\u20133 source files modified + new CLI subcommand. No behavioral change to existing execution flow \u2014 logging is additive. Enables post-hoc diagnosis of stuck or failing milestones.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Events logged during `/work-milestone` execution: `wave-start`, `wave-complete`, `item-start`, `item-complete`, `item-blocked`, `merge-attempt`, `merge-success`, `merge-conflict`, `gate-pass`, `gate-fail`\\n- [ ] Log format: JSONL \u2014 one JSON object per line with `timestamp` (ISO 8601), `event` (event type), and event-specific fields (e.g., `wave_number`, `item_ref`, `reason`)\\n- [ ] Log written to `plan/milestone-{N}-telemetry.jsonl` relative to the project root, where N is the milestone number\\n- [ ] `uv run sam telemetry report [--milestone N]` command reads the JSONL log and outputs a formatted human-readable summary (counts per event type, timeline, blocked items list)\\n- [ ] Log file is appended (not overwritten) across multiple `/work-milestone` runs on the same milestone\\n- [ ] Empty log is valid (milestone with no waves yet produces an empty file, not an error)\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 add telemetry emit instructions\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/references/` \u2014 possibly new `telemetry-events.md` reference\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/` or `packages/sam_schema/` \u2014 add `sam telemetry report` CLI command\\n- `plan/milestone-{N}-telemetry.jsonl` \u2014 runtime output (not source file)\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a developer running `/work-milestone` to orchestrate feature implementation, I need wave/item/merge events logged to `plan/milestone-{N}-telemetry.jsonl` so that I can audit execution history, diagnose blocked items, and understand merge conflict frequency.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **milestone execution telemetry logging** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Citadel assessment .claude/reports/citadel-assessment-20260320.md\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"29ce5d2e347c921233241e5d51bb7dcb614c3062dc14a7b5b515d8d43e1f4664\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTEtZg\"}"}